    "title": "Arlington Weather | News, Weather, Sports, Breaking News",
    "text": "THURSDAY, MARCH 26, 2026TODAY:Partly Sunny, BreezyHighs: 75-80Winds: Southwest 5-15, Gusts to 25 mphPeak bloom has arrived! Plan for high temperatures to soar to around 80 degrees; which is 20-degrees above normal for late March. Breezy southwest winds will increase later today ahead of a strong cold front that will bring changes tomorrow. Until then, plan for a mix of sun and clouds throughout the day with a stray shower or sprinkle not out of the question. Very warm weather is expected this evening with temperatures in the 70s.TONIGHT:Mostly CloudyShowers by DawnTemperatures: 60sWinds: Southwest 10-15+ mphIt will stay very warm overnight, with temperatures holding 60s as the cold front edges closer to the D.C. metro. Plan for breezy conditions ahead of the front, as rain develops from north to south during the overnight. Showers will likely reach the Maryland-Pennsylvania state line between 3 and 4 a.m., with rain moving inside the Beltway by around 5 a.m. A rumble of thunder is possible, and a few storms could still be on the strong side early. For the cherry blossoms around the Tidal Basin, the overnight rain and breeze may start to shake loose some petals by daybreak.FRIDAY:Rain Likely, BreezyFalling TemperaturesTemps: 60s to 50sWinds: North 5-15, Gusts to 25 mphFriday will be a much cooler, rawer day across the DMV as the cold front slowly pushes through. Temperatures will be at their warmest early in the morning, then fall steadily through the day as cooler air filters in behind the front. Expect areas rain and plenty of clouds, with afternoon readings settling into the 50s. The combination of rain, wind, and falling temperatures may start to take more of a toll on the cherry blossoms around the Tidal Basin, with more petals beginning to come down.SATURDAY:Mostly SunnyHighs: 47-52Winds: Northwest 10-15 mphA big change with blustery and noticeably colder highs only in the 40s to lower 50s. Skies trend mostly sunny, but the chill will be hard to ignore. It will be a bright day overall, though definitely jacket weather if you are heading to the Tidal Basin.SUNDAY:Sunny and BeautifulHighs: 59-64Winds: Southwest 5-10 mphSunday looks like a much nicer turnaround after the chilly start to the weekend. High pressure settles in, bringing dry conditions with a mix of sun and passing clouds. Temperatures rebound into the upper 50s to middle 60s, and with lighter winds, it should feel noticeably more comfortable. It’s a solid day to head down to the Tidal Basin before the puffy blossoms begin to fade ahead of next weeks temperatures.LOOKING AHEAD TO NEXT WEEK:The warming trend really ramps up as we head into next week. Highs climb into the 60s Monday, then push into the 70s by Tuesday, with the potential for some spots to reach the upper 70s to even low 80s by midweek. That surge in warmth will speed up the fading process for the cherry blossoms around the Tidal Basin, so the window to catch them, even in their later stages, will close quickly. A few clouds and slight rain chances may pop up at times, but the dominant story will be the return of much warmer, almost early-summer-like temperatures by the middle of the week.Download theFirst Alert Weather appand stay up to date on the latest weather news with our latest First Alert Weather blogs here.",
